%% YieldGuard — LLD 2/5: Runtime sequence, POST-MORTEM root-cause path
%% Lot X failed. Why, and what do I do?
%% Bob decides the tool order · the MCP server never calls its own tools.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Eng as Process Engineer
    participant Bob as IBM Bob (agent loop)
    participant MCP as YieldGuard MCP Server
    participant CNN as CNN Classifier (Track 1)
    participant IF as Isolation Forest (Track 2)
    participant VDB as Vector Store
    participant Tel as Simulated SECS/GEM
    participant WX as watsonx.ai (Granite)

    Eng->>Bob: Lot L-4471 came back at 61% yield. What happened?
    Note over Bob: Bob plans: need image evidence +<br/>sensor evidence before it can reason

    par Evidence gathering (independent, no ordering dependency)
        Bob->>MCP: classify_wafer_map(lot L-4471 map)
        MCP->>CNN: forward pass on 64x64 normalised map
        CNN-->>MCP: logits
        MCP-->>Bob: predicted_class:Center, confidence:0.91
    and
        Bob->>MCP: score_sensor_anomaly(lot L-4471 sensors)
        MCP->>IF: decision_function(imputed, scaled vector)
        IF-->>MCP: raw score
        MCP-->>Bob: anomaly_score:0.87,<br/>top_deviating_sensors:[sensor_12, sensor_45, ...]
    end

    alt anomaly_score >= threshold OR defect_class != None
        Note over Bob: Bob now has a defect class and a sensor<br/>signature — enough to retrieve precedent

        Bob->>MCP: retrieve_similar_cases(Center, sensor_signature, top_k=5)
        MCP->>VDB: embed(signature) -> similarity search
        VDB-->>MCP: top-k cases + confirmed_root_cause
        MCP-->>Bob: cases:[case_id:HC-018, similarity:0.88, ...]

        Bob->>MCP: query_telemetry([CMP-03], 14d)
        MCP->>Tel: parameter history window
        Tel-->>MCP: trend series
        MCP-->>Bob: telemetry:[parameter:slurry_flow_rate,<br/>direction:decreasing, magnitude_sigma:2.4]

        Note over Bob,WX: THE ORCHESTRATION POINT — Bob passes all four<br/>results in as arguments. The server does not fetch them.
        Bob->>MCP: rank_root_causes(classification, anomaly, cases, telemetry)
        MCP->>WX: fused evidence bundle + every hypothesis<br/>MUST name its evidence source constraint
        WX-->>MCP: ranked hypotheses
        MCP->>MCP: validate: reject any hypothesis whose<br/>evidence_summary names no sensor/case_id/parameter
        MCP-->>Bob: hypotheses:[hypothesis_id:H-1, description:slurry flow<br/>rate drift, confidence:0.72, evidence_summary:sensor_12 at<br/>-2.4 sigma for 6 lots · matches case HC-018, ...]

        Bob->>MCP: get_corrective_action_playbook(H-1)
        MCP->>WX: refine actions for this hypothesis
        WX-->>MCP: prioritised actions
        MCP-->>Bob: actions:[description:Verify slurry pump flow<br/>calibration on CMP-03, priority:high, ...]

        Bob-->>Eng: Ranked causes + cited evidence + corrective actions

        opt Engineer closes the loop
            Eng->>Bob: Confirmed — it was the slurry pump.
            Bob->>MCP: submit_feedback(H-1, confirmed, notes)
            MCP->>VDB: upsert verdict-tagged case
            VDB-->>MCP: ok
            MCP-->>Bob: status:ok
            Bob-->>Eng: Logged — this case now informs future retrievals
        end

    else anomaly_score < threshold AND defect_class == None
        Bob-->>Eng: Lot is within normal range on both image and sensor<br/>evidence. No root-cause analysis warranted.
        Note over Bob: Graceful stop — does NOT invent a cause<br/>just because it was asked a why question
    end

    opt Any MCP tool fails (NFR: graceful degradation)
        MCP-->>Bob: error:vector store unreachable
        Bob-->>Eng: Reports the gap and returns partial evidence.<br/>Never substitutes a confident-sounding guess.
    end
